{
  "name": "Gray-Scott Lineages: heredity",
  "description": "Four walled circles, each painted with a different Gray-Scott behaviour and seeded to found its own lineage: spots (top left), worms (top right), maze (bottom left) and curly, churning waves (bottom right). Closed, each lineage fills its circle with its own pattern. Then open doors with the Unwall tool (key 8) whenever you like: lineages that leave carry their F and k with them, so a maze lineage stays a maze inside the spots circle, and so on. Where lineages overlap their traits blend, so hybrids appear at contact zones. In the lab, with all four doors opened at 30k steps: by 150k the maze lineage held its circle and much of the ground between, curly held its own circle, spots held about 60% of theirs and spread into the worms circle, and worms disappeared (worms grow slowest). Tint = each spot's own feed.",
